    "reviewed522_mathematical_checks": {
      "status": "passed",
      "analytic_count": 22,
      "direct_analytic_review_obligations": {
        "compact-connected-setting": "h is Hermitian on a connected compact manifold; genuine potentials have finite real supremum and are finite almost everywhere.",
        "fixed-data": "The same nonzero nonnegative L1 density f is used for every exponent; no moving measure is substituted.",
        "existence-equivalence": "An exact solution is a subsolution, while the retained greatest-solution theorem makes a genuine subsolution sufficient.",
        "finite-positive-exact-mass": "For each solution, exp(lambda u)f has finite positive integral, using its finite supremum and its volume-null pole set.",
        "negative-shift": "Subtracting max(0,sup u) gives s<=0 and exp(lambda0 s)<=exp(lambda0 u).",
        "constant-invariance": "Subtracting a finite constant preserves genuineness, admissibility and the extended Monge-Ampere measure.",
        "exponent-direction": "For s<=0 and lambda>=lambda0, exp(lambda s)<=exp(lambda0 s); the inequality direction is upward solvability.",
        "upper-set-interval": "For any lambda above the nonempty set infimum, a smaller admitted exponent exists. A positive endpoint may or may not be included; zero is never included.",
        "positive-threshold": "The retained positive-threshold corollary supplies every positive exponent; no converse is claimed.",
        "conditional-zero-sequence": "Collapse assumes exact solutions along exponents decreasing to zero. It does not supply them for an arbitrary zero-threshold density.",
        "normalized-potential": "v_j=u_j-sup u_j remains genuine h-psh with supremum zero.",
        "fixed-nonpluripolar-measure": "The fixed finite measure f dV does not charge pluripolar sets, permitting the retained normalized exponential damping lemma.",
        "L1-damping": "g_j=exp(lambda_j v_j)f converges to f in L1 without potential convergence or a positive lower-mass hypothesis.",
        "nonzero-damped-density": "A genuine quasi-psh potential is finite dV-almost everywhere, so g_j is nonzero and integrable.",
        "threshold-comparison": "The exact equality MA(v_j)=c_j g_j dV gives 0<c_j<=b_h(g_j) by maximal subsolution characterization, with no equality of c_j and b_h(g_j) asserted.",
        "upper-semicontinuity": "The retained L1 upper semicontinuity theorem gives limsup c_j<=b_h(f)=0; positivity completes the limit.",
        "total-variation": "A positive finite measure has total variation equal to its mass. The mass bound c_j integral f tends to zero, and constant invariance gives the same normalized mass.",
        "logarithmic-collapse": "log c_j=lambda_j sup u_j tends to minus infinity; no rate for c_j is deduced.",
        "uniform-exponential": "At poles the exponential is zero and everywhere it is between zero and c_j, giving uniform convergence.",
        "uniform-upper-collapse": "Eventually lambda_j<1 and log c_j<0; sup u_j<=log c_j tends to minus infinity. This is distinct from normalized-potential convergence.",
        "full-parameter-consequence": "The statement along all decreasing sequences gives the full lambda-downarrow0 conclusion for any solution family when existence holds for all positive exponents.",
        "S03-application-boundary": "The tailored 521 family supplies the existence premise. Its fixed barrier mass CV0 and collapsing exact masses are compatible, since potential order does not imply total-mass order for nonclosed backgrounds."
